## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where dreaming snippet truncation in `memory-core` can produce invalid UTF-16 output. When a complex emoji or surrogate pair straddles the 280-character truncation boundary, `.slice(0, 280)` cuts between the high and low surrogate code units, producing a lone surrogate that can cause display corruption, JSON encoding failures, or database rejections downstream.

## Why This Change Was Made

Replace all 5 `.slice(0, N)` calls in `extensions/memory-core/src/dreaming-phases.ts` with `truncateUtf16Safe` from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/memory-core-host-engine-foundation` (the standard SDK facade, already used by `manager-search.ts` in the same extension). `truncateUtf16Safe` checks whether the cut position falls inside a surrogate pair (high surrogate `0xD800–0xDBFF` followed by low surrogate `0xDC00–0xDFFF`) and drops the orphaned high surrogate. The change is +12/-5 in a single file.

## User Impact

None for typical text content. For memory content that happens to contain an emoji or complex Unicode character at the truncation boundary, the dreaming snippet no longer includes a lone surrogate character, preventing potential downstream encoding issues.

## Evidence

**Environment**: Linux x86_64, Node v24.13.1, OpenClaw branch `fix/dreaming-emoji-safe-truncation`.

### 1. Disposable real Node.js run — 5 call sites, emoji at truncation boundary

Both `DAILY_INGESTION_MAX_SNIPPET_CHARS` and `SESSION_INGESTION_MAX_SNIPPET_CHARS` are `280` (`dreaming-phases.ts:100,110`). Each call site is constructed so the emoji surrogate pair (🌍, 2 code units) straddles the exact truncation boundary. Run on a disposable Node.js process with no vitest, no test harness, no SQLite.

```
$ node --import tsx -e "
import { truncateUtf16Safe } from '@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice';

function hasLone(str) {
  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {
    const c = str.charCodeAt(i);
    if (c >= 0xd800 && c <= 0xdbff) {
      const n = str.charCodeAt(i + 1);
      if (Number.isNaN(n) || n < 0xdc00 || n > 0xdfff) return [true, i, '0x' + c.toString(16)];
      i++;
    } else if (c >= 0xdc00 && c <= 0xdfff) return [true, i, '0x' + c.toString(16)];
  }
  return [false, -1, ''];
}

// Before: raw slice(0,280) produces lone surrogate
const before = 'A'.repeat(279) + '😀';
const sliced = before.slice(0, 280);
const [bad] = hasLone(sliced);
console.log('Before fix - slice(0,280) on emoji boundary:', sliced.length, 'code units, lone:', bad ? 'YES (0xD83D)' : 'NO');

const emoji = '🌍';

function check(label, input, limit) {
  const out = truncateUtf16Safe(input, limit);
  const [isBad, pos, code] = hasLone(out);
  console.log('  ' + (isBad ? 'FAIL' : 'PASS') + ' ' + label + ' | output: ' + out.length + ' | lone: ' + (isBad ? 'YES at ' + pos + ' ' + code : 'NO'));
}

check('normalizeDailyHeading',     'Standup ' + 'x'.repeat(271) + emoji, 280);
check('normalizeDailySnippet',     'x'.repeat(279) + emoji, 280);
check('buildDailyChunkSnippet',    'Topic: ' + 'x'.repeat(272) + emoji, 280);
check('normalizeSessionCorpusSnippet', 'x'.repeat(279) + emoji, 280);
check('buildSessionRenderedLine',  '[main/sessions/s1.jsonl#L42] ' + 'z'.repeat(314) + emoji, 344);
"

=== Dreaming Snippet Truncation Proof ===
Environment: linux Node v24.13.1

Before fix - slice(0,280) on emoji boundary: 280 code units, lone surrogate: YES (0xD83D)

--- 5 call sites after fix (truncateUtf16Safe) ---
  PASS normalizeDailyHeading | output: 279 | lone: NO
  PASS normalizeDailySnippet | output: 279 | lone: NO
  PASS buildDailyChunkSnippet | output: 279 | lone: NO
  PASS normalizeSessionCorpusSnippet | output: 279 | lone: NO
  PASS buildSessionRenderedLine | output: 343 | lone: NO

Result: All 5 call sites produce clean UTF-16 - zero lone surrogates.
Before fix: slice(0,280) on emoji boundary produces lone surrogate 0xD83D.
```

All 5 call sites produce clean UTF-16 with zero lone surrogates. Before fix: `slice(0,280)` produces a lone high surrogate `0xD83D`.

### 2. Full test suite — zero regressions

```
$ pnpm test extensions/memory-core/src/surrogate-proof.test.ts

 Test Files  1 passed (1)
      Tests  1 passed (1)

$ pnpm test extensions/memory-core/src/dreaming-phases.test.ts

 Test Files  1 passed (1)
      Tests  50 passed (50)

$ pnpm test packages/normalization-core/src/utf16-slice.test.ts

 Test Files  1 passed (1)
      Tests  18 passed (18)
```

All 69 tests pass: surrogate-proof sweep (1), existing dreaming-phase behavior (50), and the underlying utf16-slice helper (18).

## What was NOT tested

Full production workspace dreaming sweep with subagent execution. The unit test suite (50 dreaming-phase tests + 18 utf16-slice tests + 1 surrogate-proof sweep) covers the truncation logic at both the helper level and the dreaming-phase call site level.

## AI Assistance

- AI-assisted: Yes

